cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the companion paper, which is under submission."
title: "GeoLens: A Workbench for Comparing Zero-Shot Social Media Geolocation Engines"
abstract: >
  A web workbench that runs nine geolocation engine instances behind one
  interface and one API over a closed catalogue of places, fuses them at the
  post level and the user level, raises a verification flag when the two
  consensus places are more than 161 km apart, onboards a new place from an
  LLM-drafted editable profile, and scores every engine on a labelled CSV.
